From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:18:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 022/159] [ae-patch] Put the merge confirm step on one row and
 relabel the review offer as Mark session done

Reid, 2026-09-26, from screenshots of a 1100 px card: the confirm step put
the method buttons on one row and Confirm merge and Cancel on a second, and
after a merge the black "Set this session to review" button did not say what
it does.

The confirm step is now one wrapping row: the segmented method toggle (only
when the repo allows both methods, with the short labels Squash and Merge
commit; the question line keeps the full text), Confirm merge and Cancel
(outline again). In a card under 30rem the toggle takes its own row and the
two buttons share the next. The offer after a merge reads "Mark session
done", an outline button with a muted "frees a slot" hint beside it (the
tooltip says it sets the status to Review), and the success line reads
"Session marked done. Its slot is free." Merge logic, the head SHA pin, the
review offer rule of P20 and every test id are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
